# Professional Animation and Transition System

The user is experiencing "jumping" states for canvas elements because the generic interpolation logic is too simplistic and conflicts with specialized animations. This plan will implement a robust transition system.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> I am refactoring the core render loop to ensure all property changes (position, components, origin, color) are smoothly interpolated by default.

## Proposed Changes

### Rendering Engine

#### [MODIFY] [canvas-renderer.ts](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/lectvideoanalyser/MathViz/src/renderers/canvas-renderer.ts)
- **Enhanced `interpolateObjects`**: Implement a comprehensive interpolation function that handles:
    - `origin` and `components` for vectors.
    - `x`, `y` for points.
    - `from`, `to` for lines.
    - `vertices` for polygons.
    - `opacity` for all objects (fade in/out support).
    - `color` (HSL/RGB interpolation).
- **Animation Conflict Resolution**:
    - Introduce an `activeAnimations` Map in `CanvasState` to track objects currently controlled by specialized animators.
    - `interpolateObjects` will skip objects present in `activeAnimations`.
    - Update `animateVectorOperation` (and others) to register themselves in `activeAnimations`.
- **Render Loop Optimization**: Ensure the render loop correctly prioritizes interpolated states and manages the lifecycle of `activeAnimations`.

### Core App Logic

#### [MODIFY] [app.ts](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/lectvideoanalyser/MathViz/src/app.ts)
- Ensure that `animateTransition` is called before `renderBaseState` to set up the target states.
- Verify that `updatePresentationState` correctly triggers the transition window.

